<section class="page" id="p-about">
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <div class="about">
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Major</dt><dd>Management Information Systems</dd>
      <dt>Year</dt><dd>Senior &middot; Graduation date coming soon</dd>
      <dt>School</dt><dd>Western Washington University, College of Business &amp; Economics</dd>
      <dt>Based in</dt><dd>Bellingham, WA</dd>
      <dt>Contact</dt><dd>willi670@wwu.edu</dd>
      <dt>Online</dt><dd>LinkedIn &amp; Handshake links coming soon</dd>
    </dl>
    <div>
      <p>I'm Bode Williams, a senior in Management Information Systems at Western Washington University. I chose MIS because I like being the translator between the technical side of a business and the people who run it. I want to understand what a system does and also why it matters to the decision someone has to make on a Tuesday afternoon.</p>
      <p>Most of my coursework has been about putting data to work. In AI in Business (MIS 432), I analyzed how companies like Uber, Waymo, Airbnb, and Netflix turn data into decisions. I built forecasting portfolios, a Python knowledge graph, and agentic workflows in n8n. In MIS 322, I wrote Visual Basic .NET applications, from a stock trade calculator to a cost simulation tool. Outside of class I developed <strong>RecSync</strong>, a business plan for a system that forecasts traffic at the WWU Recreation Center and recommends the best times to work out.</p>
      <p>Before I was building systems, I was responsible for people. I'm an <strong>Eagle Scout</strong>, and I worked as <strong>Head Lifeguard at The Valley Athletic Club</strong>. There I led a team of guards, ran trainings, and was the person who had to stay calm when something went wrong. That job taught me that leadership mostly comes down to preparation and clear communication, and I bring that into every team project.</p>
      <p><strong>Something interesting about me:</strong> Coming soon.</p>
      <p>After graduation I'm looking for roles in business analytics, product, or information systems where I can help teams make smarter, data-driven decisions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

