  <!-- ---------- CAREER PREP ---------- -->
  <div class="cat">
    <h2>Career Preparation</h2>

    <div class="act">
      <h3>Superfeet Internship Applications <span class="pts">Points coming soon</span></h3>
      <div class="meta">Date: Summer 2026</div>
      <p>This summer I applied for two internships at Superfeet near Ferndale: Ecommerce Analytics Intern and Product Management Intern. I researched the company and each role, then wrote separate cover letters that connected my MIS coursework and leadership experience to what each team needed. Writing two letters for the same company taught me that a cover letter isn't a template. Each one has to answer the specific question each hiring manager is asking. I made sure the letters sounded like me, direct and confident, instead of generic application language. I liked how much clearer my own goals got as I wrote, because I had to explain why I actually wanted each role. The process sharpened my research, tailoring, and self-presentation skills. Every future application I send will start the same way: understand the role first, then show exactly how my experience fits it.</p>
    </div>

